This file OPTS THIS REPOSITORY IN to the ledger pipeline.

Without it, posttooluse_ledger_candidate.sh records nothing and
userpromptsubmit_ledger_drain.sh has nothing to hand over.

THE DEFAULT IS NOW ON (owner directive, 2026-08-23), and this file's previous body said the
opposite: "Enabling is therefore always a deliberate, per-repository act. Nothing in this stack
creates this file automatically, and nothing should." That was already false when it was written
-- `repo_scaffold.py --profile minimal` copies this file into every new repository, measured by
scaffolding one. A marker documenting a policy its own generator had retired is corrected here
rather than restored.

THE OLD DEFAULT'S REASON STILL BINDS FOR SOME REPOSITORIES, and it was a measurement, not a
worry: a lesson written into a student-facing repository is pushed where students read it. So
"default on" is not "everywhere". The authority is a single committed file:

    claude-agent-stack/GLOBAL-INFO/LESSONS/roster.txt

It carries [arm], [no-arm] and [no-contribute] sections with a reason on every denial, and
`doctor.py::check_lesson_roster` checks BOTH directions -- a listed repo missing its marker, and
a denied repo that has one. Edit the roster, not this file: deleting this copy turns capture off
for this repository alone and the roster check will then report it as drift, which is the
intended way to notice.

WHAT IS CAPTURED, so this is not a blank cheque: nothing is written without the model being
asked and answering. The hook only leaves a marker that something happened; the model rules on
the next prompt, "no entry" is a first-class answer, and `ledger.py` REFUSES an entry that fails
its predicates rather than warning about it.
